// fileio_cross_fs_isolation.rho — Phase 10 canonical example (10e)
//
// Demonstrates FIP §867's isolation invariant: Alice's manipulation
// of her `File` cap (including wrapping it in a revocable membrane
// forwarder) cannot affect a subordinate who obtained an independent
// cap for the same logical name.  Under slice-27 fresh-mint semantics,
// every `openFile` call yields a structurally distinct `File` agent
// with an independent kernel fd; membranes wrap SPECIFIC instances,
// not the underlying file, so revoking Alice's membrane leaves Bob's
// independently-minted cap unaffected.
//
// Simplification vs. the plan-doc's original "two Fs instances via
// stub Powerbox with distinct deployerIds" framing: under the shared-
// Fs MVP (see plan §Publication + PB-M-1 resolution 2026-07-30 in
// FIPS/fileio/.../powerbox-requirements.md), all deploys hold the
// same Fs cap, but per-open fresh-mint gives Alice and Bob distinct
// File caps.  The isolation property therefore holds without needing
// per-principal Fs instances — the powerbox would ADD per-principal
// bundles (a stronger property), but the core §867 invariant is
// exercisable via a single Fs today.
//
// Sequence:
//   1. Look up the ambient Fs.
//   2. Alice opens "shared" — receives fA (fresh cap A).
//   3. Bob opens "shared" — receives fB (fresh cap B, structurally
//      distinct from fA per slice-27 semantics).
//   4. Alice wraps fA in a `tellMembrane` forwarder + a private
//      `revoked` switch (the FIP §Ocap-patterns membrane idiom).
//   5. Pre-revoke: Alice's membrane forwards `tell()` to fA and
//      returns [true, 0].
//   6. Alice flips the revocation switch.
//   7. Post-revoke: Alice's membrane returns [false, "FSERR_REVOKED", _].
//   8. Bob calls fB!?("tell") DIRECTLY (not through Alice's
//      membrane) — receives [true, 0].  Alice's manipulation
//      invisible to Bob.
//
// Prerequisite: node publishes a bundled File named "shared".
//
// Companion regression: casper/tests/genesis/contracts/
// fileio_examples_spec.rs :: fileio_cross_fs_membrane_invisible_to_bob.

new
  rl(`rho:registry:lookup`),
  stdout(`rho:io:stdout`),
  fsCh,
  revoked,
  tellMembrane
in {
  rl!(`rho:id:zphjgsfy13h1k85isc8rtwtgt3t9zzt5pjd5ihykfmyapfc4wt3x5h`, *fsCh) |
  for(@(_, fs) <- fsCh) {
    // Alice and Bob each obtain a fresh File cap for the same
    // logical name.  Slice-27 fresh-mint guarantees fA and fB are
    // structurally distinct with independent cursors + kernel fds.
    for(@[true, fA] <- @fs!?("openFile", "shared", {"mode": "r"});
        @[true, fB] <- @fs!?("openFile", "shared", {"mode": "r"})) {

      // Alice wraps fA in a revocable membrane, retaining the
      // `revoked` switch (private, kept in Alice's scope).  A
      // subordinate holding *tellMembrane sees only the forwarder
      // method, not the switch, per spec §Ocap patterns > Membranes.
      revoked!(false) |
      contract tellMembrane(returnCh) = {
        for (@r <<- revoked) {
          match r {
            true => returnCh!([false, "FSERR_REVOKED", "capability revoked"])
            false => {
              for (@reply <- @fA!?("tell")) {
                returnCh!(reply)
              }
            }
          }
        }
      } |

      // Pre-revoke smoke: the membrane forwards to fA and returns
      // fA's tell reply.
      new preCh in {
        tellMembrane!(*preCh) |
        for(@preReply <- preCh) {
          stdout!(("Alice's membrane pre-revoke tell:", preReply)) |

          // Alice flips the revocation switch: consume the current
          // value, re-publish `true`.
          for(@_ <- revoked) {
            revoked!(true) |

            // Post-revoke: the membrane returns FSERR_REVOKED
            // without ever calling into fA.
            new postCh in {
              tellMembrane!(*postCh) |
              for(@postReply <- postCh) {
                stdout!(("Alice's membrane post-revoke tell:", postReply)) |

                // Bob calls fB directly (not through Alice's
                // membrane).  Alice's revocation is invisible to Bob:
                // fB is an independent agent with its own cursor.
                for(@bobReply <- @fB!?("tell")) {
                  stdout!(("Bob's independent cap post-Alice-revoke:", bobReply))
                  // Expected: [true, 0] — Bob's fresh cap starts
                  // at cursor 0, unaffected by anything Alice did.
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
